From f2a06adc0f5eca5b2a41d6b9d21692408b6ce854 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rhyne1012 <rhyne1012@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] boards/cubepilot/cubeorangeplus: hil variant with pwm_out_sim

The default build of the CubeOrange+ (PX4 v1.17.0) has no simulation
modules, so with SYS_HITL=1 the rcS line `pwm_out_sim start -m hil`
fails: no HIL_ACT_* parameters, no HIL_ACTUATOR_CONTROLS, no HITL.
The Pixhawk 6C gets pwm_out_sim through SIMULATOR_SIH (which selects
it); the CubeOrange+ board file enables neither.

This label variant (make cubepilot_cubeorangeplus_hil) is the default
board plus pwm_out_sim only. `ver all` on the FC reports
"Build variant: hil".
---
 boards/cubepilot/cubeorangeplus/hil.px4board | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)
 create mode 100644 boards/cubepilot/cubeorangeplus/hil.px4board

diff --git a/boards/cubepilot/cubeorangeplus/hil.px4board b/boards/cubepilot/cubeorangeplus/hil.px4board
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..54e50f8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/boards/cubepilot/cubeorangeplus/hil.px4board
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+CONFIG_MODULES_SIMULATION_PWM_OUT_SIM=y
